# Dates

Use `date-fns` for calendar math and formatting. Use `TZDate` from `@date-fns/tz` when a time zone matters. Account zones come from `accountTimeZone` in `lib/reviewSettings.ts`.

Call `new Date()` only for "right now" at the edge (a server action or page). Pass that instant into `lib/` functions so tests can pin it.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — hand-rolled zone math or locale formatting
const parts = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone }).formatToParts(now);
return new Date().toLocaleDateString();

// ✅ GOOD — date-fns, zone-aware, injectable now
const day = new TZDate(now, accountTimeZone(stored));
return format(addDays(day, delayDays), 'yyyy-MM-dd');
```

`Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone` is only for reading the browser's zone before storing it.
